atorname{sin}2t⟩$ for $t\\in [0,\\pi ].$ \nThe area of $D$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\mathrm{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\enclose{box}{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\mathrm{d}t,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x.$ Determine the missing part of the equation.\n\n*Hint: Note that $C$ is negatively oriented.*"] [17592186369427 "![](images/9e/9eb614f4f6e00c5fa03759a61d69734aa1c6eaf26d98d3c78b96052ca16162d0.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2},$ where \n\n- ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${\\mathbf{r}}_{1}(t)=-2{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.222em}\\mathbf{i}+3{t}^{3}\\hspace{0.222em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [-1,1],$ and\n\n- ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${\\mathbf{r}}_{2}(t)=-2\\hspace{0.222em}\\mathbf{i}-t\\hspace{0.222em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [-3,3].$\n\nUse Green's theorem to find the area of the region."] [17592186369448 "![](images/52/52ec0dfc4590daf9306c2389bd321acbf80f263c799fa4ddd4e5b8f662e0a2b5.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2},$ where \n\n- ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${\\mathbf{r}}_{1}(t)={t}^{5}\\hspace{0.222em}\\mathbf{i}+{t}^{4}\\hspace{0.222em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [-1,1],$ and\n\n- ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${\\mathbf{r}}_{2}(t)=-t\\hspace{0.222em}\\mathbf{i}+1\\hspace{0.222em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [-1,1].$\n\nUse Green's theorem to find the area of the region."] [17592186369462 "![](images/49/49b14da54c952d0585f7aa894d618838ddc91beb65216e0c18c014ba5ad268d7.png)\n\nSuppose that $\\mathbf{F}$ is a vector field on ${\\mathbb{R}}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=9,\\hspace{2em}{∮}_{{C}_{2}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=-4,\\hspace{2em}{∮}_{{C}_{3}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=-6,\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}$ is oriented counterclockwise and ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are oriented clockwise, calculate the value of $$\n{∮}_{∂D}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}.\n$$"] [17592186369469 "![](images/b3/b3562daf036c74c1472931a626d41f28de81e723377597700342823d7f2d1ac2.png)\n\nSuppose that $\\mathbf{F}$ is a vector field on ${\\mathbb{R}}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=1,\\hspace{2em}{∮}_{{C}_{2}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=7,\\hspace{2em}{∮}_{{C}_{3}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=-4,\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}$ is oriented counterclockwise and ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are oriented clockwise, calculate the value of $$\n{∮}_{∂D}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}.\n$$"] [17592186369476 "![](images/00/00edab4b102cf705ea6c65acaa61ba524e9dba5b503167d6988b2150802d9f0b.png)\n\nSuppose that $\\mathbf{F}$ is a vector field on ${\\mathbb{R}}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=7,\\hspace{2em}{∮}_{{C}_{2}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=-9,\\hspace{2em}{∮}_{{C}_{3}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are oriented counterclockwise and ${C}_{2}$ is oriented clockwise, calculate the value of $$\n{∮}_{∂D}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}.\n$$"] [17592186369483 "![](images/b2/b2754f286de30f2017974030e571ec52f85bb84ad633912922a2b514728f3a7b.png)\n\nSuppose that $\\mathbf{F}$ is a vector field on ${\\mathbb{R}}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=6,\\hspace{2em}{∮}_{{C}_{2}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=2,\\hspace{2em}{∮}_{{C}_{3}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=-10,\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}$ is oriented clockwise and ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are oriented counterclockwise, calculate the value of $$\n{∮}_{∂D}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}.\n$$"] [17592186369490 "![](images/1f/1f308d1a3ecf3bd0090e22c4f70389311db4db3ff06f7038db0cf7770a8837c7.png)\n\nSuppose that $\\mathbf{F}$ is a vector field on ${\\ma